(function(){window.PhysicaRankPyqNeet_botany_microbesinhumanwelfare=[{id:"neet-2026r-q146",pn:146,y:"Re-NEET 2026 \xB7 21 Jun",tp:"Microbes in Human Welfare",st:"Microbes as medicine",q:"Which of the following is used as a clot buster?",o:["Penicillin","Cyclosporin A","Statins","Streptokinase"],c:3,s:`Streptokinase is produced by the bacterium Streptococcus.
It is modified by genetic engineering.
It is used as a clot-buster to remove clots from blood vessels.
It helps patients who have had myocardial infarction (heart attack).`},{id:"neet-2025-q103",pn:103,y:"NEET 2025",tp:"Microbes in Human Welfare",st:"Fermented beverages",q:"Which of the following is an example of non-distilled alcoholic beverage produced by yeast?",o:["Whisky","Brandy","Beer","Rum"],c:2,s:`Wine and beer are produced without distillation.
Whisky, brandy and rum are produced by distillation of the fermented broth.`},{id:"neet-2025-q105",pn:105,y:"NEET 2025",tp:"Microbes in Human Welfare",st:"Streptokinase as clot buster",q:"Streptokinase produced by bacterium Streptococcus is used for",o:["Curd production","Ethanol production","Liver disease treatment","Removing clots from blood vessels"],c:3,s:`Streptokinase produced by the bacterium Streptococcus and modified by genetic engineering is used as a clot buster.
It removes clots from blood vessels of patients who have had a myocardial infarction (heart attack).
Curd production is done by Lactobacillus and ethanol production by Saccharomyces.`},{id:"neet-2024-q122",pn:122,y:"NEET 2024 \xB7 5 May",tp:"Microbes in Human Welfare",st:"Microbial products",q:`Match List I with List II
List I:
(A) Clostridium butylicum
(B) Saccharomyces cerevisiae
(C) Trichoderma polysporum
(D) Streptococeus sp
List II:
(I) Ethanol
(II) Streptokinase
(III) Butyric acid
(IV) Cyclosporin-A
Choose the correct answer from the options given below :`,o:["A-III, B-I, C-IV, D-II","A-IV, B-I, C-III, D-II","A-III, B-I, C-II, D-IV","A-II, B-IV, C-III, D-I"],c:0,s:`A. Clostridium butylicum gives butyric acid.
B. Saccharomyces cerevisiae gives ethanol.
C. Trichoderma polysporum gives cyclosporin-A.
D. Streptococcus sp. gives streptokinase.
So: A-III, B-I, C-IV, D-II.`},{id:"neet-2022-q132",pn:132,y:"NEET 2022 \xB7 17 Jul",tp:"Microbes in Human Welfare",st:"Nitrogen fixing microbes",q:"Which one of the following produces nitrogen fixing nodules on the roots of Alnus?",o:["Frankia","Rhodospirillum","Beijerinckia","Rhizobium"],c:0,s:`Frankia forms nitrogen fixing nodules on roots of non-leguminous plants.
Alnus is one such plant.`},{id:"neet-2022-q158",pn:158,y:"NEET 2022 \xB7 17 Jul",tp:"Microbes in Human Welfare",st:"Biofortification",q:"Breeding crops with higher levels of vitamins and minerals or higher proteins and healthier fats is called :",o:["Bio-remediation","Bio-fortification","Bio-accumulation","Bio-magnification"],c:1,s:`Breeding crops for more vitamins, minerals, protein and healthier fats is biofortification.
Biomagnification is the rise in concentration of a toxicant at successive trophic levels.
Bioremediation is using living organisms to handle pollution.`},{id:"neet-2022-q174",pn:174,y:"NEET 2022 \xB7 17 Jul",tp:"Microbes in Human Welfare",st:"Bioactive molecules from microbes",q:"Identify the microorganism which is responsible for the production of an immunosuppressive molecule cyclosporin A :",o:["Clostridium butylicum","Aspergillus niger","Streptococcus cerevisiae","Trichoderma polysporum"],c:3,s:`Cyclosporin A is an immunosuppressive agent used in organ transplants.
It is produced by the fungus Trichoderma polysporum.`},{id:"neet-2022r-q185",pn:185,y:"Re-NEET 2022 \xB7 4 Sep",tp:"Microbes in Human Welfare",st:"Spirulina and microbes",q:`Given below are two statements : one is labelled as Assertion (A) and the other is labelled as Reason (R).
Assertion (A) : Spirulina is a microbe that can be used for reducing environmental pollution.
Reason (R) : Spirulina is a rich source of protein, carbohydrates, fats, minerals and vitamins.
In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below :`,o:["(A) is not correct but (R) is correct","Both (A) and (R) are correct and (R) is the correct explanation of (A)","Both (A) and (R) are correct but (R) is not the correct explanation of (A)","(A) is correct but (R) is not correct"],c:2,s:`Spirulina is a blue-green alga that photosynthesises and adds oxygen to its surroundings.
It can be grown on starch-rich waste water (potato processing, straw, molasses), so it helps reduce pollution.
It is also rich in protein, carbohydrates, fats, minerals and vitamins.
Both are correct, but the nutrient richness does not explain the pollution control.`},{id:"neet-2020-q022",pn:22,y:"NEET 2020 \xB7 13 Sep",tp:"Microbes in Human Welfare",st:"Sewage treatment",q:"Which of the following is put into anaerobic sludge digester for further sewage treatment ?",o:["Floating debris","Effluents of primary treatment","Activated sludge","Primary sludge"],c:2,s:`After secondary treatment the flocs are settled as activated sludge.
A part is returned as inoculum and the rest goes to anaerobic sludge digesters.`},{id:"neet-2020-q031",pn:31,y:"NEET 2020 \xB7 13 Sep",tp:"Microbes in Human Welfare",st:"Microbes in industrial products",q:`Match the following columns and select the correct option.
(a) Clostridium butylicum  (i) Cyclosporin-A
(b) Trichoderma polysporum  (ii) Butyric Acid
(c) Monascus  (iii) Citric Acid
(d) Aspergillus niger  (iv) Blood cholesterol lowering agent`,o:["(a) \uF0AE (ii) ; (b) \uF0AE (i) ; (c) \uF0AE (iv) ; (d) \uF0AE (iii)","(a) \uF0AE (i) ; (b) \uF0AE (ii) ; (c) \uF0AE (iv) ; (d) \uF0AE (iii)","(a) \uF0AE (iv) ; (b) \uF0AE (iii) ; (c) \uF0AE (ii) ; (d) \uF0AE (i)","(a) \uF0AE (iii) ; (b) \uF0AE (iv) ; (c) \uF0AE (ii) ; (d) \uF0AE (i)"],c:0,s:`Clostridium butylicum - butyric acid.
Trichoderma polysporum - cyclosporin A.
Monascus - blood cholesterol lowering agent.
Aspergillus niger - citric acid.`},{id:"neet-2020-q046",pn:46,y:"NEET 2020 \xB7 13 Sep",tp:"Microbes in Human Welfare",st:"Animal husbandry breeding",q:"By which method was a new breed 'Hisardale' of sheep formed by using Bikaneri ewes and Marino rams?",o:["Mutational breeding","Cross breeding","Inbreeding","Out crossing"],c:1,s:`Hisardale was formed by crossing Bikaneri ewes with Marino rams.
Crossing superior males of one breed with superior females of another is cross breeding.`},{id:"neet-2019-q031",pn:31,y:"NEET 2019 \xB7 5 May",tp:"Microbes in Human Welfare",st:"Industrial products",q:"Which one of the following equipments is essentially required for growing microbes on a large scale, for industrial production of enzymes?",o:["Industrial oven","Bioreactor","BOD incubator","Sludge digester"],c:1,s:"Microbes are grown in large vessels called bioreactors for large-scale enzyme production."},{id:"neet-2019-q032",pn:32,y:"NEET 2019 \xB7 5 May",tp:"Microbes in Human Welfare",st:"Microbes in household and industrial products",q:`Match the following organisms with the products they produce:
(a) Lactobacillus (i) Cheese
(b) Saccharomyces cerevisiae (ii) Curd
(c) Aspergillus niger (iii) Citric Acid
(d) Acetobacter aceti (iv) Bread
(v) Acetic Acid
Select the correct option`,o:["(a)-(iii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(v), (d)-(i)","(a)-(ii), (b)-(i), (c)-(iii), (d)-(v)","(a)-(ii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(v), (d)-(iii)","(a)-(ii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(iii), (d)-(v)"],c:3,s:`Lactobacillus turns milk into curd.
Saccharomyces cerevisiae is used to make bread.
Aspergillus niger gives citric acid.
Acetobacter aceti gives acetic acid.
So (a)-(ii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(iii), (d)-(v).`},{id:"neet-2019-q048",pn:48,y:"NEET 2019 \xB7 5 May",tp:"Microbes in Human Welfare",st:"Biocontrol agents",q:"Which of the following can be used as a biocontrol agent in the treatment of plant disease?",o:["Anabaena","Lactobacillus","Trichoderma","Chlorella"],c:2,s:`Trichoderma is a free-living fungus of root ecosystems.
It controls several plant pathogens, so it is a biocontrol agent.`},{id:"neet-2019-q065",pn:65,y:"NEET 2019 \xB7 5 May",tp:"Microbes in Human Welfare",st:"Bioactive molecules",q:"Concanavalin A is :",o:["a lectin","a pigment","an alkaloid","an essential oil"],c:0,s:`Concanavalin A is a protein that binds sugars.
Such proteins are called lectins.`},{id:"neet-2019-q071",pn:71,y:"NEET 2019 \xB7 5 May",tp:"Microbes in Human Welfare",st:"Bioactive molecules",q:"Which of the following is a commercial blood cholesterol lowering agent ?",o:["Streptokinase","Lipases","Cyclosporin A","Statin"],c:3,s:`Statins come from the yeast Monascus purpureus.
They block the enzyme that makes cholesterol, so blood cholesterol falls.
Streptokinase removes clots and cyclosporin A is an immunosuppressant.
Note: The paper prints no solution; this working is added here.`},{id:"neet-2019-q077",pn:77,y:"NEET 2019 \xB7 5 May",tp:"Microbes in Human Welfare",st:"Biocontrol agents",q:"Select the correct group of biocontrol agents",o:["Oscillatoria, Rhizobium, Trichoderma","Nostoc, Azospirillium, Nucleopolyhedrovirus","Bacillus thuringiensis, Tobacco mosaic virus, Aphids","Trichoderma, Baculovirus, Bacillus thuringiensis"],c:3,s:`Trichoderma is a fungus, baculovirus a virus and Bacillus thuringiensis a bacterium, and all are used as biocontrol agents.
Oscillatoria, Rhizobium, Nostoc and Azospirillum are biofertilisers.
Tobacco mosaic virus is a plant pathogen and aphids are pests.
Note: The paper prints no solution; this working is added here.`},{id:"neet-2018-q158",pn:158,y:"NEET 2018 \xB7 6 May",tp:"Microbes in Human Welfare",st:"Curd",q:"Conversion of milk to curd improves its nutritional value by increasing the amount of",o:["Vitamin D","Vitamin A","Vitamin B\u2081\u2082","Vitamin E"],c:2,s:`Lactic acid bacteria (LAB) set milk into curd.
They also increase vitamin B\u2081\u2082 in the curd, which improves its nutritional value.
Note: The paper prints no solution; this working is added here.`},{id:"neet-2017-q096",pn:96,y:"NEET 2017 \xB7 7 May",tp:"Microbes in Human Welfare",st:"Microbes and products",q:"Which of the following is correctly matched for the product produced by them ?",o:["Sacchromyces cerevisiae : Ethanol","Acetobacter aceti : Antibiotics","Methanobacterium : Lactic acid","Penicillium notatum : Acetic acid"],c:0,s:`Yeast (Saccharomyces cerevisiae) ferments sugar to ethanol.
Acetobacter aceti makes acetic acid, Methanobacterium makes methane, and Penicillium notatum makes penicillin.
So only the first pair is correct.`},{id:"neet-2017-q102",pn:102,y:"NEET 2017 \xB7 7 May",tp:"Microbes in Human Welfare",st:"Sewage treatment",q:"Which of the following in sewage treatment removes suspended solids ?",o:["Sludge treatment","Tertiary treatment","Secondary treatment","Primary treatment"],c:3,s:`Primary treatment is physical: filtration and sedimentation.
It removes floating and suspended solids.
Secondary treatment is biological and removes organic matter.`}]})();
